;; What moved this time, and why it is not a bug:
;;
;; 1. THE STREAM PARTITION (ADR-0171, rulings A1/C1/E1/F1). Until this
;;    arc the engine had exactly ONE java.util.Random and consumption
;;    order was GLOBAL EVENT ORDER, so every draw site shared one
;;    sequence. `run` now derives FIVE streams by family -- :patient
;;    (keyed by arrival ordinal), :person, :world, :facility, :emission
;;    -- as (mix64 (mix64 seed family-tag) id-tag). No draw was added or
;;    removed by that change; every draw simply reads a different
;;    position in a different sequence, which moves every sampled value
;;    in this file (personas, bed choices, attendings, delay lengths)
;;    while leaving the STRUCTURE -- five patients, a :registered then
;;    an :admission then a :discharge each, fifteen events -- exactly
;;    as it was.
;;
;; 2. THE from = to DELAY SKIP (ADR-0171 section 2(d)). `decide :delay`
;;    used to call `rand-int-in` even when :from = :to, where the draw
;;    is arithmetically dead ((.nextInt rng 1) is always 0). It is now
;;    skipped. Draw-affecting, and landed in the SAME commit as the
;;    partition on purpose (ruling F1): splitting them would have spent
;;    a second corpus-wide reshuffle to buy nothing.
;;
;; This is exactly the "generator's stochastic surface changed once, for
;; a documented reason" case sim/ADR-0009 decision 1 names and accepts.
;; The corpora that moved with it are the four arc0_gated_*.edn under
;; components/sim/test, the two conformance baselines, demos/traces'
;; fourteen captures, event-examples.edn, and all 35 regression-oracle
;; roots -- one reshuffle, all of it in one commit.
;;
;; Regenerate again -- deliberately, not casually -- the next time a
;; milestone's new step types or config surface add stochastic
;; behavior existing pathways now exercise (sim/ADR-0009's own expectation,
;; not a bug to chase). See
